# Diff CI-policy sources as text, always.
#
# Git classifies a blob as binary when it finds a control byte near the start,
# and then prints "Bin 8864 -> 9127 bytes" instead of a diff. That has hidden a
# review twice in this repository: a raw NUL concealed the stranded-merge
# payload in #1332, and NUL/SOH digest separators rendered
# scripts/lib/sdk-build-evidence.mjs -- the file deciding whether a downloaded
# build may be trusted -- as an unreadable blob to every reviewer of #1334.
#
# test/scripts/source-text-guard.test.mjs stops a control byte being committed.
# This stops one that slipped through, or one already in the *old* side of a
# diff, from taking the review with it: the fix for a binary-classified file is
# itself binary-classified without this, so the commit that repairs the problem
# is the one nobody can read.
*.mjs diff
*.cjs diff
*.mts diff
*.js diff
*.ts diff
*.tsx diff
*.yml diff
*.yaml diff
*.json diff
*.md diff
